#3500
The Moor Crossing~
   You stand on open moor, a wide, bare place where the wind howls with
nothing to stop it. Tracks cross the heather here. One wanders north toward
the hills, where few go now, for there are tales of things moving in the old
dwarf-mines beneath them. A narrow trail scars its way east up toward a
stony hillside and the farms of the ridge. A lane runs south between the
trees.
~
